{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 18, :comments ["<b>Surely</b> — The wicked in this world are as though enticed by smooth words, and in the end they become למשואות, like: שואה ומשואה לתוהו, and one who is not on the path of the wicked — to their destruction at their end." "Some say: למשואות — from the root of הנחש השיאני, and the meaning is doubled."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 73, :notes {1 "'The meaning is doubled' (והטעם כפול) likely refers to the word bearing two senses simultaneously; rendered literally without expanding."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:34:16.539050467Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}